# qcrild calls back into QtiTelephonyService over binder.
#
# Seen as, during a call:
#   avc: denied { call } for comm="DispatcherModul"
#     scontext=u:r:rild:s0 tcontext=u:r:platform_app:s0 tclass=binder
#
# QtiTelephonyService (/system_ext/app/QtiTelephonyService, shared user
# android.uid.qtiphone) is platform-signed, so it lands in platform_app, and it
# is the only bridge from qcrild's IQcRilAudio to the audio HAL. Denied under
# enforcing, calls connect but carry no audio - the same silent-call symptom as
# when the service fails to start.
#
# The reverse direction is already allowed by the core policy; this is the
# callback qcrild makes into it.
binder_call(rild, platform_app)
